/T (The recent evolution of language models, which enable contextual and semantic representations of text, has enhanced the effectiveness of text clustering. Language is more than a bag of words, and recent language models have proved to be quite capable of capturing that notion. Text clustering, unbound by supervision, allows for creative solutions and diverse applications, such as finding outliers, speedup labeling, and finding incorrectly labeled data.)
