/Title (Text clustering has also found itself in the realm of topic modeling, where we want to discover \(abstract\) topics that appear in large collections of textual data. As shown in Figure 5-2, we generally describe a topic using keywords or keyphrases and, ideally, have a single overarching label.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 502 0 R
/Next 535 0 R
>>
endobj
533 0 obj
<<
/Title (These approaches generally use a bag-of-words technique for the main features of the textual data, which does not take the context nor the meaning of words and phrases into account. In contrast, our text clustering example does take both into account as it relies on Transformer-based embeddings that are optimized for semantic similarity and contextual meaning through attention.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 536 0 R
/Next 503 0 R
>>
endobj
